/.prompt/
/docs/
# What is kept out is what has one developer's own choices burned into it — which agent to run,
# which editor to use — because those are the clone's to make, not ours to hand down. A helper
# tool with none of that in it is published instead, however far it sits from the build. So they
# live here alongside the tree, ignored.
/.claude/
/.zed/
# Whatever is one developer's own — the scripts that drive their own Windows box over ssh, the
# PowerShell gate whose only subject those are, and `.local/local.mk`, the seam `make` includes
# when it is present, where a target for any of them belongs. A clone builds, tests and ships
# amenbo without any of it. It is a directory rather than a list of names so that placing a file
# decides which side it is on, and nothing rests on remembering a suffix.
/.local/
/target/
# Tauri sidecar staging: `make gui`/`gui-dev` build the CLI and drop it here as
# `amenbo-<triple>` for bundle.externalBin. Build artifact, not source.
/app/src-tauri/binaries/
# wharfy: the distribution state/artifact area (`.wharfy/`) and the prebuilt binaries `make dist`
# emits (`dist/`). Both are distribution artifacts, not source. The wharfy config `wharfy.yaml` is
# committed.
/.wharfy/
/dist/

# amenbo: the dir→store/project pointer (`.amenbo`). store_id points at machine-specific app-data, so
# it is not committed (it is invalid on a clone). The store itself and the secrets are not here; they
# live in app-data. `.amenbo-home/` is an unused legacy pointer dir, kept ignored defensively.
.amenbo
.amenbo-home/
# AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md are placed by the AI-agent environment of whoever clones this repo (`amenbo
# init` generates the managed block). Which agent anyone uses is not ours to decide, so it is not
# committed.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
# The PII denylist plaintext (real names/emails/accounts) is managed outside the repo. Committing it
# would burn the very thing it protects into the tree = a self-leak.
.pii-denylist
